DTV C-to-Rust Translation Dataset
=================================

This directory contains C source programs and differential-testing inputs used
in the C-to-Rust evaluation of the DTV (Decoding Time Verification) framework.

Per-case contents:
  source.c       Original C program.
  testcases/*    Differential-testing standard-input files.
  metadata.json  Construction record (tool versions, parameters, counts).

Source attribution
------------------

The C programs in `source.c` are derived from IBM Project CodeNet:

  Project CodeNet: A Large-Scale AI for Code Dataset for Learning a
  Diversity of Coding Tasks.
  Ruchi Puri, David S. Kung, Geert Janssen, Wei Zhang, Giacomo Domeniconi,
  Vladmir Zolotov, Julian Dolby, Jie Chen, Mihir Choudhury, Lindsey Decker,
  Veronika Thost, Luca Buratti, Saurabh Pujar, Ulrich Finkler.
  NeurIPS 2021 Datasets and Benchmarks Track.
  https://github.com/IBM/Project_CodeNet
  arXiv:2105.12655

Project CodeNet is distributed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
(see ./LICENSE).

Selection and filtering applied to CodeNet for this dataset is documented in
Appendix E of the DTV paper:

  - Filter to C submissions with status `Accepted` that read standard input
    (scanf, fgets, getchar, ...).
  - Per problem retain the median-byte-size submission.
  - Stratified-sample 400 candidates by source byte size, run the AFL++
    pipeline (LLM seed generation, fuzzing, minimization, sanitizer filter),
    and uniformly sample 300 from the 306 successful outputs.

Generated content (this work)
-----------------------------

The following per-case content is produced by our pipeline rather than copied
from CodeNet, and is released under the same Apache License 2.0 as the
underlying source programs:

  testcases/*    Differential-testing inputs generated via LLM-seeded AFL++
                 fuzzing followed by sanitizer filtering.
  metadata.json  Pipeline configuration, tool versions, and per-stage counts.

The AFL++ pipeline that produces these files is maintained in a separate
repository (`agent_fuzz`) and is not included here.
